{"type":"system","subtype":"hook_response","hook_id":"43984c3b-b3a8-49e5-af4e-c2ea25114736","hook_name":"UserPromptSubmit","hook_event":"UserPromptSubmit","output":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\": {\"hookEventName\": \"UserPromptSubmit\", \"additionalContext\": \"[free-hands: entry] The prompt mentions free-hands. If it asks to run something in free-hands mode, ask exactly one question first, in the user's language, before any reasoning or work: \\\"Enter free-hands mode?\\\" (yes/no). Claude Code: AskUserQuestion. Codex: ask it as a plain question and end the turn. On the next turn: yes \\u2192 start the mode with the goal from the earlier prompt (Claude Code: the Skill tool, skill `free-hands:run`; Codex: read /Users/jeonjelyong/WorkSpace/Z-Work/z-lab/free-hands-lab/run-0.1.0/subject/free-hands/skills/run/SKILL.md and follow it); no \\u2192 propose possible directions and end the turn without doing the work. A mention that explains, quotes or looks back at free-hands is not a request \\u2014 answer it normally. When unsure, ask the entry question.\"}}\n","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\": {\"hookEventName\": \"UserPromptSubmit\", \"additionalContext\": \"[free-hands: entry] The prompt mentions free-hands. If it asks to run something in free-hands mode, ask exactly one question first, in the user's language, before any reasoning or work: \\\"Enter free-hands mode?\\\" (yes/no). Claude Code: AskUserQuestion. Codex: ask it as a plain question and end the turn. On the next turn: yes \\u2192 start the mode with the goal from the earlier prompt (Claude Code: the Skill tool, skill `free-hands:run`; Codex: read /Users/jeonjelyong/WorkSpace/Z-Work/z-lab/free-hands-lab/run-0.1.0/subject/free-hands/skills/run/SKILL.md and follow it); no \\u2192 propose possible directions and end the turn without doing the work. A mention that explains, quotes or looks back at free-hands is not a request \\u2014 answer it normally. When unsure, ask the entry question.\"}}\n","stderr":"","exit_code"