{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbZX8C9rtgN5CC8YcVWD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"늦게 도착한 devils-advocate 응답(A 유지)을 저장하고, 결정 기록에 반영합니다."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4022,"cache_read_input_tokens":66715,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4022},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"52908836-360b-4fc1-8c3b-7ec2cfdd48d4","uuid":"73840b4d-2aec-4a4e-a68a-a3a0e1269b7a","timestamp":"2026-10-01T13:02:04.343Z","request_id":"req_011CfbZX7oLu3jXRDaT4bWig"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbZW63AAV3i5ExMbJFEU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```json\n{\"option\": \"A\", \"new_option\": \"\", \"reasons\": [\"The repo has no dependency setup at all: no pyproject.toml, requirements*.txt, setup.py or setup.cfg, and no tools/ directory yet. With click or typer, the first change has to set up dependency management (a manifest, a venv or install step, and a pinning policy). Without that setup, `python tools/report.py` on a fresh machine or a new Python install fails with ModuleNotFoundError. With argparse, the tool is one file that runs on any Python 3.11 interpreter.\", \"Over years with one maintainer, the main ongoing cost is upkeep, not the first write. A third-party library means watching releases, bumping pins and following deprecations. Click 8.x has removed or deprecated APIs within its major line. Typer is still pre-1.0, depends on click (plus rich and shellingham in the default distribution) and has broken when click released. So typer stacks two upgrade streams on one person. Stdlib argparse changes slowly, moves only when the interpreter moves, and deprecates over several releases.\", \"Three subcommands fit easily in argparse: `add_subparsers(dest=..., required=True)` with one `set_defaults(func=...)` per subparser. That is about 15-25 lines more than click decorators. This is a fixed cost, paid once, and it is no reason to take on a dependency.\", \"Typer's main selling point is inferring the CLI from type hints. For three subcommands that saves little, and it hides behavior (how bool/Optional/list map to flags, rich-formatted errors) that a lone maintainer has to relearn years later. argparse puts the whole CLI shape in plain calls in one file.\", \"If A turns out wrong, it is cheap to undo. The parser lives in one file of a small tool, so moving to click later is a local rewrite of maybe 50 lines with no data or interface migration. Going the other way does not undo cleanly: once click or typer is in, the packaging scaffolding added for it stays.\", \"argparse is easy to test: write `main(argv: list[str] | None = None)` and call it directly in tests with a list, no CliRunner needed.\"], \"evidence\": [{\"claim\": \"The repo has no Python packaging or dependency manifest and no tools/ directory; only .git and .free-hands exist\", \"source\": \"Glob of /private/var/folders/jx/81xz9_xj7x31h6mwxd7qrlj40000gn/T/free-hands-lab-c04/repo (pyproject.toml, requirements*.txt, setup.py, setup.cfg, tools/** all absent)\"}, {\"claim\": \"The goal only asks to decide the CLI library and record it under ## Decisions; it gives no requirement for rich output, shell completion or plugins\", \"source\": \"/private/var/folders/jx/81xz9_xj7x31h6mwxd7qrlj40000gn/T/free-hands-lab-c04/repo/.free-hands/goal.md:7\"}, {\"claim\": \"Stdlib argparse provides add_subparsers and set_defaults, which cover subcommand dispatch with no extra dependency (checked in the local 3.13 stdlib, not 3.11)\", \"source\": \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.12_1/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/lib/python3.13/argparse.py:1448,1873\"}, {\"claim\": \"The brief names one maintainer for years, Python 3.11, and three subcommands\", \"source\": \"/private/var/folders/jx/81xz9_xj7x31h6mwxd7qrlj40000gn/T/free-hands-lab-c04/repo/.free-hands/panel/01-cli/brief.json:17-19\"}], \"risks\": [\"Not verified here (no web access): that typer is still 0.x, that its default install pulls in rich and shellingham, and that some click 8.2-era releases broke typer. These claims come from memory.\", \"Not verified here: the details of click's in-major deprecations (for example around BaseCommand/MultiCommand and CliRunner mix_stderr).\", \"No Python 3.11 interpreter was found locally, so the argparse API was checked against the 3.13 stdlib. add_subparsers(required=True) has existed since 3.7, so 3.11 should be fine.\", \"If the tool later needs shell completion, colored help, prompts or nested command groups, argparse needs more hand-written code. Python 3.14 adds colored help to argparse, but the 3.11 constraint does not get it.\", \"The brief does not say whether the wider project (outside this lab repo) already uses click. If it does, the dependency cost under B mostly goes away.\"], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"would_change_if\": \"I would switch to B (click, never C) if the repo already has a dependency manifest or virtualenv workflow with click in it, or if the tool's requirements grow to shell completion, interactive prompts or nested command groups.\"}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":233,"cache_read_input_tokens":10167,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":233,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018PnU6GoLWjKNsdcstg1X9M","session_id":"52908836-360b-4fc1-8c3b-7ec2cfdd48d4","uuid":"dd3c348d-b9d4-44a4-8ca8-17a6ce64c5a6","timestamp":"2026-10-01T13:02:07.641Z","request_id":"req_011CfbZW5eLDD9BvUDTvpn4C","subagent_type":"free-hands:deep-thinker","task_description":"Panel: deep-thinker"}
